security. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Candidate Profile Education MSc, Engineering Degree, or equivalent qualification in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Bioinformatics, Data Engineering, or a related field. Technical Skills ·         Strong Python development skills. ·         Experience building APIs using FastAPI, Flask, or similar frameworks. ·         Experience with SQL, NoSQL, and vector databases. ·         Experience with Docker/Singularity and containerized environments. ·         Familiarity with Linux systems and software engineering best practices. ·         Experience developing and operating production-quality software. ·         Experience with monitoring, logging, tracing, and observability tools. ·         Knowledge of MLOps practices, CI/CD, and AI deployment workflows. Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience operating machine learning or LLM-based systems in production. ·         Experience with ML Observability and AI infrastructure. ·         Familiarity with OpenTelemetry, or similar tools. ·         Experience monitoring model performance, data quality, and drift. ·         Experience implementing evaluation frameworks for LLMs, RAG systems, or AI agents. ·         Experience with Kubernetes and cloud-native technologies. ·         Experience working with biomedical, healthcare, or other regulated data environments. Personal Skills ·         Strong problem-solving abilities. ·         Rigorous and quality-oriented mindset. ·         Ability to work independently while collaborating within multidisciplinary teams. ·         Strong communication skills. ·         Interest in research and innovation. Why Join Us ? AGORA offers a unique opportunity to help shape the next generation of AI systems for oncology by working on real-world scientific and clinical challenges alongside leading researchers and physicians. The project brings together several of the most exciting areas of modern artificial intelligence, including large language models (LLMs), multi-agent systems, knowledge graphs, multi-omics data integration, biological modelling, and clinical decision support. Beyond technology development, the ambition is to explore how agentic AI can become a genuine scientific partner—capable of reasoning over complex biomedical data, integrating up-to-date medical knowledge, supporting molecular interpretation, and generating novel research hypotheses. At the intersection of fundamental research, data science, systems biology, and precision medicine, Institut Curie provides a world-class research environment with access to unique clinical and molecular datasets. You will work within a highly interdisciplinary team and benefit from significant scientific freedom, opportunities for high-impact publications, international collaborations, and participation in the development of future national and European research initiatives. Contract Information Contract type: Fixed-term contract (CDD) Starting date: As soon as possible Duration: 18 months Salary: According to experience and institutional salary scales Benefits: Subsidized staff restaurant, public transportation reimbursement (70%), Private health insurance, Hybrid work opportunities Location: Institut Curie, Paris, France Application Send CV, cover letter, referees Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact h28jnhvrd35k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations 