    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/fxwmd4gdzk": {
      "title": "Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Research Engineer (M/F)",
      "description": "Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Research Engineer (M/F) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Research Engineer (M/F) (F/H) Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The “Institut Curie” is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Contexte Institut Curie is recruiting a Research Engineer or Scientist in Artificial Intelligence to join the AGORA project (AGentic Orchestration for Research and Clinical Applications in Oncology). The ambition of AGORA is to design and validate one of the first agentic AI platforms fully dedicated to biomedical research and precision oncology. The platform will be capable of exploring complex biological data, integrating the latest medical knowledge, assisting molecular interpretation, and generating novel research hypotheses. To achieve this goal, AGORA combines large language models (LLMs), biomedical knowledge bases, bioinformatics tools, multi-omics datasets, and clinical data into a unified reasoning framework. The project brings together experts in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data science, specialists in health data integration and governance, researchers in systems biology and mechanistic modelling, as well as oncologists actively involved in precision medicine programmes. The successful candidate will work at the interface of these different groups and will join the Bioinformatics Core Facility and INSERM U1331 Computational Oncology Unit, a highly interdisciplinary environment comprising approximately 100 researchers working in computational biology, bioinformatics, and artificial intelligence. Main Responsabilities The position is central to the project and aims to develop the scientific and technological foundations of a new generation of AI assistants for oncology. As a Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Engineer (M/F), you will: ·         Design and develop multi-agent architectures for biomedical applications. ·         Evaluate and benchmark large language models and agentic AI frameworks. ·         Develop workflows integrating: ◦         multi-step reasoning, ◦         Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), ◦         bioinformatics and biological modelling tools, ◦         machine learning and predictive AI models. ·         Connect AI agents with biomedical knowledge bases, analysis pipelines, and HPC resources. ·         Define evaluation protocols assessing response quality, explainability, robustness, and reliability. ·         Collaborate closely with biologists, clinicians, bioinformaticians, and data engineers. ·         Contribute to scientific publications and future research projects in AI and precision oncology. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Candidate Profile Education ·         PhD (or equivalent experience) in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a related field. Technical Skills ·         Excellent Python programming skills. ·         Strong experience with generative AI and large language models. ·         Experience with agentic AI systems or complex orchestration architectures. ·         Good knowledge of information retrieval methods, RAG systems, vector databases, and/or knowledge graphs. ·         Familiarity with Linux environments and modern software development practices. Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience with LangGraph/LangChain, CrewAI, MCP, or similar frameworks. ·         Experience in biology, genomics, digital health, biomedical research, or oncology. ·         Scientific publications in AI, machine learning, bioinformatics, or computational biology. Personal Skills ·         Scientific curiosity. ·         Innovative mindset. ·         Ability to work autonomously. ·         Interest in interdisciplinary research. ·         Ability to transform exploratory ideas into robust and reusable solutions. Why Join Us ? AGORA offers a unique opportunity to help shape the next generation of AI systems for oncology by working on real-world scientific and clinical challenges alongside leading researchers and physicians. The project brings together several of the most exciting areas of modern artificial intelligence, including large language models (LLMs), multi-agent systems, knowledge graphs, multi-omics data integration, biological modelling, and clinical decision support. Beyond technology development, the ambition is to explore how agentic AI can become a genuine scientific partner—capable of reasoning over complex biomedical data, integrating up-to-date medical knowledge, supporting molecular interpretation, and generating novel research hypotheses. At the intersection of fundamental research, data science, systems biology, and precision medicine, Institut Curie provides a world-class research environment with access to unique clinical and molecular datasets. You will work within a highly interdisciplinary team and benefit from significant scientific freedom, opportunities for high-impact publications, international collaborations, and participation in the development of future national and European research initiatives. Contract Information Contract type: Fixed-term contract (CDD) Starting date: As soon as possible Duration: 18 months Salary: According to experience and institutional salary scales Benefits: Subsidized staff restaurant, public transportation reimbursement (70%), Private health insurance, Hybrid work opportunities Location: Institut Curie, Paris, France Application Send CV, cover letter, referees Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact fxwmd4gdzk5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 18 mois Quotité de travail Référence fxwmd4gdzk Publié le 26/08/2026 Postuler Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Research Engineer (M/F) (F/H) Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The “Institut Curie” is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Contexte Institut Curie is recruiting a Research Engineer or Scientist in Artificial Intelligence to join the AGORA project (AGentic Orchestration for Research and Clinical Applications in Oncology). The ambition of AGORA is to design and validate one of the first agentic AI platforms fully dedicated to biomedical research and precision oncology. The platform will be capable of exploring complex biological data, integrating the latest medical knowledge, assisting molecular interpretation, and generating novel research hypotheses. To achieve this goal, AGORA combines large language models (LLMs), biomedical knowledge bases, bioinformatics tools, multi-omics datasets, and clinical data into a unified reasoning framework. The project brings together experts in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data science, specialists in health data integration and governance, researchers in systems biology and mechanistic modelling, as well as oncologists actively involved in precision medicine programmes. The successful candidate will work at the interface of these different groups and will join the Bioinformatics Core Facility and INSERM U1331 Computational Oncology Unit, a highly interdisciplinary environment comprising approximately 100 researchers working in computational biology, bioinformatics, and artificial intelligence. Main Responsabilities The position is central to the project and aims to develop the scientific and technological foundations of a new generation of AI assistants for oncology. As a Generative AI and Multi-Agent Systems Engineer (M/F), you will: ·         Design and develop multi-agent architectures for biomedical applications. ·         Evaluate and benchmark large language models and agentic AI frameworks. ·         Develop workflows integrating: ◦         multi-step reasoning, ◦         Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), ◦         bioinformatics and biological modelling tools, ◦         machine learning and predictive AI models. ·         Connect AI agents with biomedical knowledge bases, analysis pipelines, and HPC resources. ·         Define evaluation protocols assessing response quality, explainability, robustness, and reliability. ·         Collaborate closely with biologists, clinicians, bioinformaticians, and data engineers. ·         Contribute to scientific publications and future research projects in AI and precision oncology. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Candidate Profile Education ·         PhD (or equivalent experience) in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a related field. Technical Skills ·         Excellent Python programming skills. ·         Strong experience with generative AI and large language models. ·         Experience with agentic AI systems or complex orchestration architectures. ·         Good knowledge of information retrieval methods, RAG systems, vector databases, and/or knowledge graphs. ·         Familiarity with Linux environments and modern software development practices. Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience with LangGraph/LangChain, CrewAI, MCP, or similar frameworks. ·         Experience in biology, genomics, digital health, biomedical research, or oncology. ·         Scientific publications in AI, machine learning, bioinformatics, or computational biology. Personal Skills ·         Scientific curiosity. ·         Innovative mindset. ·         Ability to work autonomously. ·         Interest in interdisciplinary research. ·         Ability to transform exploratory ideas into robust and reusable solutions. Why Join Us ? AGORA offers a unique opportunity to help shape the next generation of AI systems for oncology by working on real-world scientific and clinical challenges alongside leading researchers and physicians. The project brings together several of the most exciting areas of modern artificial intelligence, including large language models (LLMs), multi-agent systems, knowledge graphs, multi-omics data integration, biological modelling, and clinical decision support. Beyond technology development, the ambition is to explore how agentic AI can become a genuine scientific partner—capable of reasoning over complex biomedical data, integrating up-to-date medical knowledge, supporting molecular interpretation, and generating novel research hypotheses. At the intersection of fundamental research, data science, systems biology, and precision medicine, Institut Curie provides a world-class research environment with access to unique clinical and molecular datasets. You will work within a highly interdisciplinary team and benefit from significant scientific freedom, opportunities for high-impact publications, international collaborations, and participation in the development of future national and European research initiatives. Contract Information Contract type: Fixed-term contract (CDD) Starting date: As soon as possible Duration: 18 months Salary: According to experience and institutional salary scales Benefits: Subsidized staff restaurant, public transportation reimbursement (70%), Private health insurance, Hybrid work opportunities Location: Institut Curie, Paris, France Application Send CV, cover letter, referees Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact fxwmd4gdzk5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste : CDD Durée du contrat : 18 mois Référence fxwmd4gdzk Publié le 26/08/2026 L'Université PSL (Paris Sciences & Lettres) Menu Footer RH CGU Crédits Politique de confidentialité Flux RSS de PSL Recrutement Gestion des cookies Vos paramètres de cookies Vous naviguez sur le site de l’Université PSL. L’Université PSL, responsable de traitement, utilise des cookies pour la réalisation de statistiques ainsi que pour l’optimisation du site. Vous pouvez accepter ou refuser l’utilisation de cookies, ainsi que personnaliser vos préférences. Nous conservons votre choix pendant 3 mois. Vous pouvez changer d’avis à tout moment en cliquant sur l’icône « Gestion des cookies » en bas à gauche sur toutes les pages de notre site internet. Plus d'informations Cookies obligatoire (session Drupal) Ces cookies sont strictement obligatoires au bon fonctionnent du site. Cookies vidéos Ils permettent la visualisation des vidéos sur notre site. (Youtube) Cookies de mesure d'audience Enregistrer mes choix Tout accepter Personnaliser"
