    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/22l6v6w519": {
      "title": "Ingénieur d’étude en recombinaison homologue (F/H)",
      "description": "Ingénieur d’étude en recombinaison homologue (F/H) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Ingénieur d’étude en recombinaison homologue (F/H) (F/H) Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil Institut Curie Research Center is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a Hospital group and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales The laboratory The successful candidate will join the Compartmentalization and Dynamics of Nuclear Functions team led by Angela Taddei at Institut Curie ( https://curie.fr/equipe/taddei ). Our research focuses on understanding how nuclear organization regulates genome functions, with a particular emphasis on homologous recombination. We combine state-of-the-art in vivo quantitative microscopy approaches, including super-resolution imaging, with genetic and molecular biology techniques. The project This position is part of a project aimed at studying the various stages of the DNA damage response (DDR) in relation to genome spatial organization in the yeast S. cerevisiae . The missions : The recruited engineer will have two main responsabilities : -         The individual will strengthen the team’s capacity to generate new yeast strains required for the project’s progress (tool construction : plasmids and strains) -         He/she will adapt the oligopaint tcehnique to vizualize 3D chromosome conformation during the DNA damage response. This part of the project will be carried out with the assistance of a reserach engineer from the Taddei team and a research engineer from the Curie Coretech platform. As part of his duties, the engineer will conduct experiments, analyzeresults, maintain an up-to-date electronic laboratory notebook, and present project progress at laboratory meetings. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Education and experience -         Professional Bachelor’s degree or Master 2 -         Experience in molecular biology and microscopy Required skills and qualities -        Theoretical and practical knowledge of standard techniques in molecular biology (PCR, cloning, probe labeling) and cell biology (immunostaining, fluorescence microscopy). -        Familiarity with image acquisition and analysis software (Metamorph, Fiji). -        Ability to analyze results and synthesize information. -        Good interpersonal skills and ability to work in a team. -        Strong motivation to learn interdisciplinary techniques and work in a collaborative environment. -        Proficiency in English is required, as it is the laboratory’s working language. Contract information Type of contract : Fixed-term contract. Starting date: Position available immediately Duration : 9 months Working time : full time Remuneration : according to the current grids Benefits : Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV and letter of motivation Publication date: 22/07/2026 Deadline for application: until filled Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+3, Bac+4, Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact 22l6v6w5195k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Rémunération De 27232.83 à 29240.67 € (Euros) par an Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 9 mois Quotité de travail Référence 22l6v6w519 Publié le 22/07/2026 Postuler Ingénieur d’étude en recombinaison homologue (F/H) (F/H) Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil Institut Curie Research Center is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a Hospital group and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales The laboratory The successful candidate will join the Compartmentalization and Dynamics of Nuclear Functions team led by Angela Taddei at Institut Curie ( https://curie.fr/equipe/taddei ). Our research focuses on understanding how nuclear organization regulates genome functions, with a particular emphasis on homologous recombination. We combine state-of-the-art in vivo quantitative microscopy approaches, including super-resolution imaging, with genetic and molecular biology techniques. The project This position is part of a project aimed at studying the various stages of the DNA damage response (DDR) in relation to genome spatial organization in the yeast S. cerevisiae . The missions : The recruited engineer will have two main responsabilities : -         The individual will strengthen the team’s capacity to generate new yeast strains required for the project’s progress (tool construction : plasmids and strains) -         He/she will adapt the oligopaint tcehnique to vizualize 3D chromosome conformation during the DNA damage response. This part of the project will be carried out with the assistance of a reserach engineer from the Taddei team and a research engineer from the Curie Coretech platform. As part of his duties, the engineer will conduct experiments, analyzeresults, maintain an up-to-date electronic laboratory notebook, and present project progress at laboratory meetings. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Education and experience -         Professional Bachelor’s degree or Master 2 -         Experience in molecular biology and microscopy Required skills and qualities -        Theoretical and practical knowledge of standard techniques in molecular biology (PCR, cloning, probe labeling) and cell biology (immunostaining, fluorescence microscopy). -        Familiarity with image acquisition and analysis software (Metamorph, Fiji). -        Ability to analyze results and synthesize information. -        Good interpersonal skills and ability to work in a team. -        Strong motivation to learn interdisciplinary techniques and work in a collaborative environment. -        Proficiency in English is required, as it is the laboratory’s working language. Contract information Type of contract : Fixed-term contract. Starting date: Position available immediately Duration : 9 months Working time : full time Remuneration : according to the current grids Benefits : Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV and letter of motivation Publication date: 22/07/2026 Deadline for application: until filled Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal opportunity employer and is dedicated to the highest standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+3, Bac+4, Bac+5 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact 22l6v6w5195k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Rémunération : De 27232.83 à 29240.67 € (Euros) par an Type de contrat / de poste : CDD Durée du contrat : 9 mois Référence 22l6v6w519 Publié le 22/07/2026 L'Université PSL (Paris Sciences & Lettres) 